    {
      "text": "deceitfulness of riches, choke the word, Matt. 13:22 (Mark 4:19). that no man deceive you, Matt. 24:4 (Mark 13:5; Luke 21:8). saying, I am Christ; and shall deceive many, Matt. 24:5 (Mark 13:6; JS—M 1:6). false Christs … shall deceive the very elect, Matt. 24:24 (JS—M 1:22). others said … he deceiveth the people, John 7:12. Are ye also deceived, John 7:47. fair speeches deceive the hearts of the simple, Rom. 16:18. Let no man deceive himself, 1 Cor. 3:18. Be not deceived, 1 Cor. 6:9 (15:33). such are false apostles, deceitful workers, 2 Cor. 11:13. Be not deceived; God is not mocked, Gal. 6:7. whereby they lie in wait to deceive, Eph. 4:14. corrupt according to the deceitful lusts, Eph. 4:22. Let no man deceive you with vain words, Eph. 5:6. Beware lest any man spoil you through … vain deceit, Col. 2:8. Let no man deceive you by any means, 2 Thes. 2:3 (1 Jn. 3:7). Adam was not deceived, 1 Tim. 2:14. evil men … deceiving, and being deceived, 2 Tim. 3:13. not hearers only, deceiving your own selves, James 1:22. say that we have no sin, we deceive ourselves, 1 Jn. 1:8. many deceivers are entered into the world, 2 Jn. 1:7. Satan, which deceiveth the whole world, Rev. 12:9. by thy sorceries were all nations deceived, Rev. 18:23. he should deceive the nations no more, Rev. 20:3. devil that deceived them was cast into the lake, Rev. 20:10.",
